# Exhaustiveness: the summary block must be EXACTLY this. Any extra
# application section or changed resource fails here rather than being
# quietly pinned by the next --regenerate.
# No resources= : the target side never rendered, so nothing moved.
expect:affected=1 changed=0 errors=1
# The target's kustomization cannot build, and the failure is report content -
# the app errors, the run does not.
must:# Error: failed to render target branch
# The diagnosis is the point: it is what the two rewrites below exist to make
# visible, and it sat behind ~17,000 characters of flags in the report that
# motivated them.
must:cycle detected
# 1. The cluster's API-version set must reach the report as a COUNT. ArgoCD
#    passes one --helm-api-versions pair per advertised group/version AND kind
#    and quotes the whole argv into the failure; util/kustomize, unlike
#    util/helm, does not strip it from the error it RETURNS.
must:--helm-api-versions <N elided>
#    The negative is the one that actually catches a regression: two adjacent
#    pairs mean the list came back. It cannot be satisfied by the elided form,
#    which contains exactly one pair.
must-not:--helm-api-versions [^ ]+ --helm-api-versions
# 2. The render root must be redacted, as ArgoCD redacts it in the command list
#    it returns. `kustomize build` is quoted with an ABSOLUTE app path and
#    kustomize names absolute paths in its own diagnoses, so an unredacted error
#    puts an ephemeral worktree directory in a PR comment three times. Pinned
#    POSITIVELY: the placeholder the normalizer would leave behind is banned by
#    the review gate itself, so only the redacted spelling can be asserted here.
must:kustomize build \./apps/kustomize-helm
